## Exact changes

### (1) [`sw.js:1`](sw.js:1) — versioned cache name
```
- const cacheName = "clock";
+ const cacheName = "clock-v2";
```

### [`sw.js:31–41`](sw.js:31) — activate handler added between `install` and `fetch`
```js
self.addEventListener("activate", (e) => {
    e.waitUntil(
        caches.keys().then((keys) =>
            Promise.all(
                keys.filter((key) => key !== cacheName).map((key) => caches.delete(key))
            )
        ).then(() => self.clients.claim())
    );
});
```
Deletes every cache not named `"clock-v2"`, then calls `self.clients.claim()` so existing offline clients immediately adopt the new service worker and receive the updated `src/*.js` files.

---

### (2) [`src/records.js:31`](src/records.js:31) — `settled` flag added
```js
+ var settled = false;
```
[`src/records.js:46–48`](src/records.js:46):
```js
  req.onerror = function () {
+     if (settled) return;
+     settled = true;
      reject(req.error);
  };
```
Prevents `reject()` from being called more than once if multiple concurrent IDB requests fire `onerror`.

### [`test/records.test.js:152–172`](test/records.test.js:152) — two new tests
`collectTaskRecords resolves with [] when tasks is null` and `…when tasks is undefined` — both pass `null`/`undefined` and assert `deepEqual(records, [])`. Existing 4 tests are untouched.

---

### (3) [`index.js:907`](index.js:907) — unknown custom element replaced
```js
- let roundEntryDuration = document.createElement("round-entry-duration");
+ let roundEntryDuration = document.createElement("div");
```
The `className` assignment on line 908 is unchanged (`"round-entry-duration"`), so CSS continues to match. Verified: no CSS rule anywhere in the project selects by the `round-entry-duration` tag name; the stylesheet uses only the `.round-entry-duration` class selector.
